-- title:
--   Idelic Artin map sends local norms at v into H'
-- statement:
--   Let $F/E$ be a Galois extension of number fields whose Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ is commutative, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ admissible for the degree $n=[F:E]$, i.e. $\mathfrak f\neq 0$ and $v^{\,\mathrm{admissibleExpOfDegree}\,E\,n\,v}\mid\mathfrak f$ for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_E$ whose chosen prime above in $F$ has nontrivial inertia subgroup. Let $r\colon (\mathbb A_E)^\times\to\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ be a group homomorphism such that: the principal idèles (the image of $E^\times$) lie in $\ker r$; $\ker r$ is the subgroup generated by the principal idèles together with the image of the idelic norm of the base change `genuineBaseChange E F`; $r$ is surjective; and for every idèle unit $u$ satisfying `IsAdjuster E 𝔣 u 1` (at each $v\mid\mathfrak f$ the finite component of $u$ is a unit with $|u_v-1|\le \exp(-\mathrm{ord}_v\mathfrak f)$, and the archimedean component of $u$ is positive at every real embedding of $E$) one has $r(u)=\prod^{f}_{v} \mathrm{artinFrob}\,E\,F\,v^{\,\mathrm{placeOrd}\,E\,(\mathrm{projFin}\,E\,u)\,v}$, the finite product over height-one primes of the arithmetic Frobenius at the prime above $v$ raised to the $v$-adic valuation of the finite part of $u$. Fix a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_E$, a unit $a\in (E_v)^\times$, and an idèle unit $x$ whose archimedean part is $1$ and whose finite component is $1$ at every prime other than $v$, with $v$-component equal to $a$. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_F$ lying under $v$, let $H'$ be a subgroup of the decomposition subgroup $D_w\le\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ of the valuation subring of $w$, and let $b\in (F_w)^\times$ be fixed by every element of $H'$ and satisfy $\prod^{f}_{c\in D_w/H'} (\mathrm{Quotient.out}\,c)\cdot b = a$ in $F_w$, the product being taken over the coset space with the chosen representatives and the right-hand side the image of $a$ under the canonical semialgebra map $E_v\to F_w$ attached to $w$ over $v$. Then $r(x)$ lies in the image of $H'$ in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$.
--
--   This is the norm condition (condition $(2')$ in Serre's axiomatic characterisation of the local reciprocity map) for the local component $a\mapsto r(\iota_v(a))$ of the idelic Artin map: elements of $E_v^\times$ that are norms from the fixed field of $H'\le D_w$ are sent into $H'$. It feeds the identification of the local components of the idelic Artin map with local reciprocity maps, and the associated computation of the kernel of $a \mapsto r(\iota_v(a))$.
